stric cancer.WU L:Wu L is an author known for conducting significant meta-analyses in the field of nutrition and cancer research. One of Wu L's notable studies focused on the relationship between dietary nitrates, nitrites, and nitrosamines intake and the risk of gastric cancer. Additionally, Wu L conducted another meta-analysis examining the association between red meat consumption and the risk of stomach cancer. Through these studies, Wu L has contributed valuable insights into dietary factors that may influence gastric cancer risk.GUAN W:Guan W is an author who conducted a meta-analysis on dietary nitrates, nitrites, and nitrosamines intake and gastric cancer risk.ABID Z:Abid Z is an author who reviewed the relationship between meat, dairy, and cancer.CROSS AJ:Cross AJ is an author who reviewed the relationship between meat, dairy, and cancer.SINHA R:Sinha R is an author who reviewed the relationship between meat, dairy, and cancer.LU M:Lu M is an author who conducted a meta-analysis on red meat consumption and stomach cancer risk.YIN Q:Yin Q is an author who conducted a meta-analysis on red meat consumption and stomach cancer risk.FU B:Fu B is an author who conducted a meta-analysis on red meat consumption and stomach cancer risk.J CANCER RES CLIN ONCOL:J Cancer Res Clin Oncol is a journal that published a meta-analysis on red meat consumption and stomach cancer risk.ZHU H:Zhu H is a researcher and author known for their contributions to the field of health and nutrition. They examined the antidepressant-like effects of sodium butyrate in combination with estrogen, exploring potential therapeutic avenues for mental health. Additionally, Zhu H conducted a meta-analysis on the relationship between red and processed meat intake and gastric cancer risk, providing valuable insights into dietary impacts on cancer development. Through these studies, Zhu H has contributed significantly to understanding both mental health treatments and dietary influences on cancer risk.