e and the risk of gastric cancer. Additionally, Zhang C conducted a study focused on the association between meat consumption and the risk of esophageal cancer. Through these studies, Zhang C has contributed valuable insights into the potential health risks associated with different types of meat consumption."}{"title": "DIG DIS SCI:DIG DIS SCI, also known as Digestive Diseases and Sciences, is a journal that focuses on research in the field of gastroenterology. It has published studies on various topics, including a significant study that examined the relationship between meat consumption and the risk of esophageal cancer. This journal serves as a platform for disseminating important findings and advancements in digestive health and related diseases."}{"title": "SONG P:Song P is an author known for conducting meta-analyses on dietary factors and their association with gastric cancer risk. Specifically, Song P has investigated the intake of dietary nitrates, nitrites, and nitrosamines, as well as the consumption of red meat, in relation to stomach cancer risk. Through these studies, Song P has contributed valuable insights into the potential dietary influences on gastric cancer."}{"title": "WU L:Wu L is an author known for conducting significant meta-analyses in the field of nutrition and cancer research. One of Wu L's notable studies focused on the relationship between dietary nitrates, nitrites, and nitrosamines intake and the risk of gastric cancer. Additionally, Wu L conducted another meta-analysis examining the association between red meat consumption and the risk of stomach cancer. Through these studies, Wu L has contributed valuable insights into dietary factors that may influence gastric cancer risk."}{"title": "GUAN W:Guan W is an author who conducted a meta-analysis on dietary nitrates, nitrites, and nitrosamines intake and gastric cancer risk."}{"title": "ABID Z:Abid Z is an author who reviewed the relationship between meat, dairy, and cancer."}{"title": "CROSS AJ:Cross AJ is an author who reviewed the relationship between meat, dairy, and cancer."}{"title": "SINHA R:Sinha R is an author who reviewed the relationship between meat, dairy, and cancer."}{"title": "LU M:Lu M is an author who conducted a meta-analysis on red meat consumption and stomach cancer risk."}{"title": "YIN Q:Yin Q is an author who conducted a meta-analysis on red meat consumption and stomach cancer risk."}{"title": "FU B:Fu B is an author who conducted a meta-analysis on red meat consumption and stomach cancer risk."}{"title": "J CANCER RES CLIN ONCOL:J Cancer Res Clin Oncol is a journal that published a meta-analysis on red meat consumption and stomach cancer risk."}{"title": "ZHU H:Zhu H is a researcher and author known for their contributions to the field of health and nutrition. They examined the antidepressant-like effects of sodium butyrate in combination with estrogen, exploring potential therapeutic avenues for mental health. Additionally, Zhu H conducted a meta-analysis on the relationship between red and processed meat intake and gastric cancer risk, providing valuable insights into dietary impacts on cancer development. Through these studies, Zhu H has contributed significantly to understanding both mental health treatments and dietary influences on cancer risk."}{"title": "ZHU C:Zhu C is an author who conducted a meta-analysis on red and processed meat intake and gastric cancer risk."}{"title": "TAO G:Tao G is an author who conducted a meta-analysis on red and processed meat intake and gastric cancer risk."}{"title": "ZHAO L:Zhao L is an author who conducted a meta-analysis on red and processed meat intake and gastric cancer risk."}{"title": "JOHNSON CM:Johnson CM is an author who conducted meta-analyses of colorectal cancer risk factors."}{"title": "WEI C:Wei C is an author who conducted meta-analyses of colorectal cancer risk factors."}{"title": "ENSOR JE:Ensor JE is an author who conducted meta-analyses of colorectal cancer risk factors."}{"title": "SMOLENSKI DJ:Smolenski DJ is an author who conducted meta-analyses of colorectal cancer risk factors."}{"title": "AMOS CI:Amos CI is an author who conducted meta-analyses of colorectal cancer risk factors."}{"title": "LEVIN B:Levin B is an author who conducted meta-analyses of colorectal cancer risk factors."}{"title": "XU X:Xu X is an author who conducted a meta-analysis on red and processed meat intake and colorectal adenomas."}{"title": "YU E:Yu E is an author who conducted a meta-analysis on red and processed meat intake and colorectal adenomas."}{"title": "GAO X:Gao X is an author who conducted a meta-analysis on red and processed meat intake and colorectal adenomas."}{"title": "SONG N:Song N is an author who conducted a meta-analysis on red and processed meat intake and colorectal adenomas."}{"title": "LIU L:Liu L is an author recognized for their contributions to medical research, particularly in the field of risk factors associated with symptomatic hyponatremia, as detailed in a publication in the Intern Med J. Additionally, Liu L has conducted a meta-analysis examining the relationship between red and processed meat intake and the occurrence of colorectal adenomas. Through these studies, Liu L has contributed valuable insights to the understanding of dietary impacts on health and disease."}{"title": "WEI X:Wei X is an author who conducted a meta-analysis on red and processed meat intake and colorectal adenomas."}{"title": "ZHANG W:Zhang W is"}{"title": "J AM COLL NUTR:Journal of the American College of Nutrition publishes research on nutrition and its impact on health."}{"title": "JPN J CLIN ONCOL:Japanese Journal of Clinical Oncology publishes research related to clinical oncology and cancer treatment in Japan."}{"title": "BR J CANCER:British Journal of Cancer is a peer-reviewed journal that publishes research on cancer and its treatment."}{"title": "NUTR J:NUTR J, also known as Nutrition Journal, is an open-access journal dedicated to publishing research focused on nutrition and dietary practices. The journal covers a wide range of topics related to nutrition, including its effects on health and disease. Notably, it includes studies on parenteral nutrition specifically for surgical patients, highlighting its commitment to advancing knowledge in the field of nutrition and its critical role in health management."}{"title": "MED ONCOL:Medical Oncology is a journal that publishes research on the treatment of cancer with medical therapies."}{"title": "ASIAN PAC J CANCER PREV:Asian Pacific Journal of Cancer Prevention publishes research on cancer prevention in the Asian Pacific region."}{"title": "OBES REV:Obesity Reviews (OBES REV) is a journal dedicated to publishing systematic reviews and research on obesity-related topics. It focuses on various aspects of obesity, including dietary fiber and its implications for health. The journal serves as a platform for disseminating knowledge about obesity and its associated health issues, contributing to the understanding and management of this significant public health concern."}{"title": "HEPATOCELLULAR CARCINOMA:Hepatocellular carcinoma is a primary malignancy of the liver and is recognized as a type of liver cancer that frequently arises in patients with liver cirrhosis. This condition is often linked to various dietary and lifestyle factors, which can contribute to its development. Hepatocellular carcinoma is significant in the context of liver diseases, accounting for approximately 30% of deaths related to these conditions, particularly among individuals suffering from liver cirrhosis. Additionally, it is important to consider nutritional support during the treatment of hepatocellular carcinoma, as patients may experience increased energy expenditure due to the disease."}{"title": "LUNG CANCER:Lung cancer is a type of cancer that begins in the lungs, with research exploring its links to meat consumption."}{"title": "BREAST CANCER:Breast cancer is a type of cancer that develops from breast tissue. It is a significant area of study, particularly concerning its risk factors, which include various dietary intakes. Numerous studies have been conducted to examine the relationship between dietary factors and the risk of developing breast cancer, highlighting the importance of nutrition in understanding this disease."}{"title": "OVARIAN CANCER:Ovarian cancer is a type of cancer that originates in the ovaries. Research has been conducted to explore various dietary factors that may influence the risk of developing this disease. Specifically, studies have examined the association between meat consumption and ovarian cancer, as well as the impact of fish intake on its risk. These investigations aim to better understand how different dietary habits may contribute to the development of ovarian cancer."}{"title": "BLADDER CANCER:Bladder cancer is a type of cancer that affects the bladder, originating from the cells within this organ. Research has been conducted to explore various factors that may influence the risk of developing bladder cancer, including dietary influences such as fish consumption. These studies aim to better understand the relationship between diet and the incidence of this disease, highlighting the importance of nutrition in cancer risk assessment."}{"title": "PROSTATE CANCER:Prostate cancer is a type of cancer that occurs in the prostate gland, often studied in relation to dietary habits."}{"title": "NON-HODGKIN LYMPHOMA:Non-Hodgkin lymphoma is a type of cancer that originates in the lymphatic system, with research exploring dietary links."}{"title": "GLIOMA:Glioma is a type of tumor that occurs in the brain and spinal cord, with studies examining dietary associations."}{"title": "ORAL CAVITY AND OROPHARYNX CANCER:Oral cavity and oropharynx cancer refers to cancers that occur in the mouth and throat, often studied in relation to dietary factors."}{"title": "COLORECTAL CANCER:Colorectal cancer is a type of cancer that originates in the colon or rectum. Research has indicated a potential link between dietary factors and the risk of developing this disease. Specifically, studies suggest that higher intake of dietary fiber may reduce the risk of colorectal cancer. Additionally, various studies have explored the relationship between fish consumption and the risk of this type of cancer, highlighting the importance of diet in influencing colorectal cancer risk."}{"title": "MEAT CONSUMPTION:"}{"title": "RED AND PROCESSED MEAT:"}{"title": "MEAT INTAKE:"}{"title": "PROCESSED MEAT:"}{"title": "DIETARY FIBRE:Dietary fibre is a type of carbohydrate that the body cannot digest. It plays a significant role in digestive health and may also have an impact on chronic diseases, such as Chronic Obstructive Pulmonary Disease (COPD)."}{"title": "NUTR METAB CARDIOVASC DIS:NUTR METAB CARDIOVASC DIS, also known as Nutrition, Metabolism and Cardiovascular Diseases, is a journal dedicated to the research and publication of studies focusing on the interplay between nutrition, metabolism, and cardiovascular health. The journal emphasizes the impact of nutrition on cardiovascular diseases and aims to advance understanding in this critical area of health. It serves as a platform for disseminating research that explores the relationship between dietary factors and cardiovascular well-being, contributing to the broader field of cardiovascular disease research."}{"title": "AM J CARDIOL:The American Journal of Cardiology publishes articles on cardiovascular disease and related topics."}{"title": "COCHRANE DATABASE SYST REV:The Cochrane Database of Systematic Reviews is a comprehensive database that offers systematic reviews of healthcare interventions. It focuses on synthesizing primary research related to human health care and policy, providing valuable insights and evidence-based information for healthcare professionals and policymakers. The database is renowned for its rigorous methodology and commitment to high-quality research, making it a critical resource in the field of healthcare."}{"title": "MEDICINE:Medicine is a journal that publishes research articles across various medical disciplines."}{"title": "WORLD J SURG ONCOL:World Journal of Surgical Oncology focuses on surgical oncology and related research."}{"title": "EUROPEAN JOURNAL OF EPIDEMIOLOGY:The European Journal of Epidemiology publishes research on epidemiology and public health."}{"title": "INTERACT C:InterAct C is a collaborative study focusing on dietary fiber and its effects on health."}{"title": "DIABETOLOGIA:Diabetologia is a scientific journal dedicated to publishing research on diabetes and its complications. The journal encompasses a wide range of studies, including those related to gut microbiota and metabolic health, reflecting its commitment to advancing knowledge in the field of diabetes. Through its publications, Diabetologia aims to contribute to the understanding and management of diabetes and its associated health issues."}{"title": "DURKE BATAGLANI:Durke Bataglani is a researcher who has contributed to studies on dietary fiber and cancer risk."}{"title": "MEGGIE TAZBAH:Meggie Tazbah is a researcher focused on the relationship between dietary fiber intake and various health risks."}{"title": "CORONARY HEART DISEASE:Coronary heart disease is a type of cardiovascular disease that is influenced by various dietary factors. Research indicates that the consumption of omega-3 fatty acids can have an impact on the condition, as well as dietary fiber intake, which has been supported by various studies. These dietary components play a significant role in the management and prevention of coronary heart disease, highlighting the importance of nutrition in cardiovascular health."}{"title": "DIETARY FIBER:"}{"title": "YE EQ:Ye EQ is an author who contributed to research on dietary fiber and its effects on health, particularly in relation to type 2 diabetes and cardiovascular disease."}{"title": 