butions to both cancer research and the understanding of muscle loss in patients undergoing liver transplantation."}{"title": "ZHENG JS:Zheng JS is a researcher who has studied the intake of fish and cancer risk."}{"title": "HU XJ:Hu XJ is a researcher involved in studies on dietary factors and cancer risk."}{"title": "ZHAO YM:Zhao YM is a researcher who has studied the relationship between n-3/n-6 PUFAs and cancer risk."}{"title": "YANG J:Yang J is a co-author of a study published in the International Journal of Surgery, which investigates the effect of early oral feeding on the short-term outcomes of patients undergoing laparoscopic distal gastrectomy. In addition to this work, Yang J is also a researcher engaged in studies that explore the impact of dietary factors on cancer risk."}{"title": "BMC CANCER:BMC Cancer is a peer-reviewed medical journal dedicated to publishing research articles related to cancer. It encompasses a wide range of topics, including meta-analyses, systematic reviews, and studies focusing on nutritional outcomes in cancer patients. Notably, BMC Cancer has also published the study protocol for the PROPILS trial, further contributing to the body of research in the field of oncology."}{"title": "AMERICAN JOURNAL OF CLINICAL NUTRITION:The \"American Journal of Clinical Nutrition\" is a leading, peer-reviewed journal dedicated to publishing original research and reviews in the field of clinical nutrition. It focuses on the effects of nutrition on health and disease, encompassing a wide range of topics including obesity, dietary intake, and various health outcomes. The journal features studies related to specific dietary components, such as dairy consumption, dietary fat intake, calcium, phosphorus, and copper metabolism, as well as their implications for disease risk, including cancer and heart disease.\n\nThe American Journal of Clinical Nutrition serves as a vital resource for researchers and practitioners in the field of nutrition and dietetics, providing insights into the dietary management of conditions like phenylketonuria and metabolic disorders. By publishing research on the impact of nutrition on health, the journal contributes significantly to the understanding of how dietary choices influence overall well-being and the prevention of chronic diseases."}{"title": "INTERNATIONAL JOURNAL OF CLINICAL PRACTICE:The International Journal of Clinical Practice is a peer-reviewed journal dedicated to publishing research on clinical practices and guidelines in the field of medicine. It focuses on various aspects of clinical research and practice, including studies related to cancer risk and dietary factors. The journal serves as a platform for disseminating important findings that can influence clinical practices and improve patient care."}{"title": "NUTRITION CANCER:Nutrition Cancer is a journal dedicated to exploring the intricate relationship between nutrition and cancer. It publishes a wide range of research, including studies that examine the impact of dietary factors, such as dairy products, on cancer risk. The journal also focuses on dietary interventions specifically designed for cancer patients, providing insights into how nutrition can influence cancer outcomes. Additionally, Nutrition Cancer features meta-analyses that synthesize existing research on dietary factors and their association with cancer risk, contributing to a deeper understanding of how nutrition can affect cancer prevention and management."}{"title": "EUROPEAN JOURNAL OF CLINICAL NUTRITION:The European Journal of Clinical Nutrition (Eur J Clin Nutr) is a peer-reviewed journal dedicated to publishing research on various aspects of nutrition and its impact on health. It covers a wide range of topics, including inter-observer variability in body composition measurement, cancer risk studies, and the implications of clinical nutrition for health and disease. The journal also focuses on specific issues such as sarcopenia and its effects on the elderly, as well as studies and guidelines related to the management of eating disorders. Through its comprehensive research publications, the European Journal of Clinical Nutrition aims to advance the understanding of nutrition and its critical role in health outcomes."}{"title": "JAPANESE JOURNAL OF CLINICAL ONCOLOGY:The Japanese Journal of Clinical Oncology is a peer-reviewed journal that publishes research on oncology, including studies on cancer risk factors in the Japanese population."}{"title": "CANCER CAUSES & CONTROL:Cancer Causes & Control is a journal that focuses on the epidemiology and prevention of cancer, including studies on dietary factors and cancer risk."}{"title": "FISH CONSUMPTION:Fish consumption refers to the dietary intake of fish, which has been extensively studied for its health benefits. It is particularly linked to cardiovascular health due to the presence of omega-3 fatty acids found in fish. Additionally, research has explored the potential associations between fish consumption and various cancer risks. Overall, fish consumption is recognized for its significant impact on health, especially concerning heart health and cancer prevention."}{"title": "SKIN CANCER:Skin cancer refers to cancers that develop in the skin, with studies exploring the impact of omega-3 fatty acids on its risk."}{"title": "GASTRIC CANCER:Gastric cancer is a type of cancer that affects the stomach and is the focus of extensive research and clinical studies. It is associated with various complications, including chyloperitoneum, and often necessitates nutritional assessment and support for affected patients. The journal \"Gastric Cancer\" publishes research specifically dedicated to this disease, covering a wide range of topics such as surgical outcomes, treatment strategies, and nutritional guidelines for patient care. Additionally, studies have explored the influence of dietary factors, including salt intake and fish consumption, on the risk of developing gastric cancer. Overall, gastric cancer remains a significant area of study, with ongoing research aimed at improving patient outcomes and understanding the disease's complexities."}{"title": "RENAL CANCER:Renal cancer, or kidney cancer, is a type of cancer that affects the kidneys, with studies examining dietary factors such as fish consumption in relation to its risk."}{"title": "ESOPHAGEAL CANCER:Esophageal cancer is a type of cancer that affects the esophagus, the tube responsible for carrying food from the throat to the stomach. This condition is the focus of numerous studies that investigate various aspects, including nutritional support, treatment options, and surgical outcomes. Research has highlighted the significant weight loss and nutritional challenges faced by patients with esophageal cancer, prompting investigations into dietary influences, such as the impact of fish consumption on the disease. Overall, esophageal cancer presents complex challenges that are being actively studied to improve patient care and outcomes."}{"title": "BRITISH JOURNAL OF NUTRITION:The British Journal of Nutrition is a peer-reviewed journal dedicated to publishing research on nutrition and its significant impact on health. It covers a wide range of topics, including the effects of dietary fats on health, the relationship between nutrition and various health conditions, and the implications of nutritional status for health outcomes. The journal features studies on specific populations, such as stroke patients and individuals with liver cirrhosis, as well as broader research on energy expenditure and other nutritional factors. Overall, the British Journal of Nutrition serves as a vital resource for advancing knowledge in the field of nutrition and its effects on health."}{"title": "CURRENT OPINION IN LIPIDOLOGY:Current Opinion in Lipidology is a journal that provides reviews on lipid metabolism and related diseases."}{"title": "JOURNAL OF CLINICAL INVESTIGATION:Journal of Clinical Investigation is a journal that publishes research on clinical and translational medicine."}{"title": "MEDICINE AND SCIENCE IN SPORTS AND EXERCISE:Medicine and Science in Sports and Exercise is a journal that publishes research on sports medicine and exercise science."}{"title": "JOURNAL OF THE AMERICAN COLLEGE OF NUTRITION:The Journal of the American College of Nutrition is a scholarly publication that focuses on research related to nutrition and its effects on health. It encompasses a wide range of topics, including studies on exercise and dietary supplements, highlighting the integral role that nutrition plays in overall well-being."}{"title": "OBESITY RESEARCH:Obesity Research is a journal that publishes research on obesity and its related health issues."}{"title": "SWEETENED BEVERAGE CONSUMPTION:Sweetened beverage consumption refers to the intake of drinks that contain added sugars, which has been linked to various health issues, including obesity and type 2 diabetes."}{"title": "AMERICAN JOURNAL OF PUBLIC HEALTH:A peer-reviewed journal that publishes research on public health issues, including nutrition and health studies."}{"title": "ADVANCES IN NUTRITION:\"Advances in Nutrition\" is a journal dedicated to publishing both original research and comprehensive reviews focused on the field of nutrition and its significant impact on health and disease. The journal serves as a platform for disseminating valuable findings and insights that contribute to the understanding of nutritional science."}{"title": "JOURNAL OF THE AMERICAN DIETETIC ASSOCIATION:A journal that publishes research related to dietetics and nutrition, focusing on dietary practices and their effects on health."}{"title": "NATURAL REVIEWS ENDOCRINOLOGY:A journal that publishes reviews on endocrinology, including the effects of dietary components on metabolic health."}{"title": "NATIONAL HEALTH AND NUTRITION EXAMINATION SURVEY II:A survey that assesses the health and nutritional status of adults and children in the United States."}{"title": "NIPPON DATA80:A study that examines the health and nutritional status of the Japanese general population."}{"title": "DICKINSON BD:An author who has contributed to research on public health and sodium intake."}{"title": "BROWNELL KD:An author known for research on soft drink consumption and its effects on health."}{"title": "LUDWIG DS:An author who has researched the relationship between sugar-sweetened drinks and childhood obesity."}{"title": "MALIK VS:An author who has conducted systematic reviews on sugar-sweetened beverage intake and weight gain."}{"title": "CHAJES V:An author who has studied the association between fatty acids and breast cancer risk."}{"title": "FIELD AE:An author involved in research on dietary fat and weight gain among women."}{"title": "COHEN HW:An author who has researched sodium intake and its effects on mortality."}{"title": "GRAUDAL N:GRAUDAL N is an author and researcher known for conducting meta-analyses on sodium intake and its health outcomes. He has published significant research focusing on the relationship between sodium intake and mortality, contributing valuable insights to the field of nutrition and public health."}{"title": "CHILDHOOD OBESITY:A significant public health issue characterized by excessive body fat in children, often linked to dietary habits including the consumption of sugar-sweetened beverages."}{"title": "DIETARY FAT:Dietary fat refers to the types and amounts of fat that should be consumed in a child's diet, as outlined in dietary guidelines. It encompasses essential nutrients necessary for health, playing a crucial role in various bodily functions. However, it is important to note that while dietary fat is vital, excessive consumption can lead to weight gain and other health issues. Therefore, moderation and balance are key when incorporating dietary fats into a child's nutrition."}{"title": "TRANS FATTY ACIDS:Unsaturated fats that have been hydrogenated, associated with increased risk of heart disease and other health problems."}{"title": "SUGAR-SWEETENED BEVERAGES:"}{"title": "NETHERLANDS COHORT STUDY:The Netherlands Cohort Study on diet and cancer investigates dietary factors and their association with cancer risk in the Netherlands."}{"title": "DASH DIET:The DASH diet, or Dietary Approaches to Stop Hypertension, is a comprehensive dietary plan designed to help treat and prevent high blood pressure (hypertension). It emphasizes the consumption of fruits, vegetables, and low saturated fat intake, promoting specific food patterns and nutrient intake that contribute to improved cardiovascular health. The diet has been studied for its effects on urine composition and the risk of kidney stones, highlighting its focus on magnesium-rich foods, which can help reduce the saturation of calcium oxalate. Overall, the DASH diet aims to reduce hypertension and its associated health risks while also decreasing the incidence of kidney stones through its nutrient-rich food recommendations."}{"title": "KOREAN CIRCULATION JOURNAL:The Korean Circ J is a medical journal that publishes research related to cardiovascular health and diseases."}{"title": "NATIONAL INSTITUTES OF HEALTH:The National Institutes of Health (NIH) is a key agency within the U.S. Department of Health and Human Services, serving as the primary entity for conducting and supporting medical research. It is responsible for advancing biomedical and public health research, and it also sponsors various projects related to dietary evaluation technology. As the nation's medical research agency, the NIH plays a crucial role in improving health outcomes through its extensive research initiatives and funding programs."}{"title": "CANCER PREVENTION STUDY II:The Cancer Prevention Study II is a long-term study conducted by the American Cancer Society to understand the causes of cancer and the impact of lifestyle factors on cancer risk."}{"title": "SODIUM:Sodium is an essential mineral and electrolyte that plays a critical role in various bodily functions, including maintaining fluid balance and supporting nerve and muscle function. However, its intake must be carefully managed, particularly in individuals with specific health conditions. Excessive sodium consumption is linked to several health risks, including hypertension, increased cardiovascular risk, and potentially kidney stone formation. \n\nFor patients with chronic kidney disease or renal insufficiency, sodium intake should be restricted to prevent fluid retention and hypertension, with recommended limits often set between 750-1000 mg per day for those undergoing hemodialysis. Additionally, sodium's impact on urinary calcium excretion further connects it to kidney stone formation, highlighting the importance of monitoring sodium levels in the diet. Overall, while sodium is vital for health, excessive intake poses significant risks, necessitating careful dietary management, especially for vulnerable populations."}{"title": "SALT:"}{"title": "CANCER PREVENTION STUDY II NUTRITION COHORT:A cohort study focused on the relationship between dietary factors and cancer risk, particularly breast cancer."}{"title": "NORWEGIAN WOMEN AND CANCER STUDY:A prospective cohort study examining the impact of dairy consumption and calcium intake on breast cancer risk among Norwegian women."}{"title": "STANISLAS STUDY:A study investigating dairy product consumption and metabolic syndrome-related factors over a period of five years."}{"title": "HOORN STUDY:A study assessing the relationship between dairy consumption, body weight, and metabolic disturbances in a Dutch population."}{"title": "DIETARY INTERVENTION STUDY:A study designed to assess the effects of dietary changes on health outcomes, particularly in non-diabetic individuals in China."}{"title": "CANCER CAUSES AND CONTROL:A journal that focuses on the epidemiology and prevention of cancer, including studies on dietary factors and cancer risk."}{"title": "WORLD JOURNAL OF DIABETES:A journal that discusses the role of various factors, including vitamin D, in diabetes and metabolic syndrome."}{"title": "CHINA:China is a country located in East Asia, known for its extensive research on various health-related topics, including studies on sodium and potassium intake and their effects on hypertension. In these studies, it was found that the average potassium intake in China is approximately 1.8 grams per day."}{"title": "CA CANCER J CLIN:CA: A Cancer Journal for Clinicians is a peer-reviewed medical journal that provides information on cancer statistics and research."}{"title": "CANCER EPIDEMIOL BIOMARKERS PREV:Cancer Epidemiology, Biomarkers & Prevention is a journal that focuses on cancer epidemiology and prevention research."}{"title": "EUR J NUTR:European Journal of Nutrition publishes research on nutrition and its impact on health."}{"title": "CANCER DETECT PREV:Cancer Detect Prev is a publication that serves as a journal dedicated to research on cancer detection and prevention strategies. It emphasizes the importance of advancing knowledge in the field of cancer research, specifically targeting methods and approaches for early detection and preventive measures against cancer."}{"title": "EURO HEART J:European Heart Journal is a leading journal in cardiovascular medicine, publishing research on heart diseases and treatments."}{"title": "GBD 2013 MORTALITY AND CAUSES OF DEATH COLLABORATORS:The GBD 2013 Mortality and Causes of Death Collaborators is a group that conducts research on global health metrics, including mortality and causes of death."}{"title": "DAIRY:Dairy products are food items derived from milk, which are often studied for their nutritional value and potential health impacts, including cancer risk."}{"title": "COLON CANCER:Colon cancer is a type of cancer that affects the colon and is a significant focus of medical research, particularly in relation to dietary factors."}{"title": "CANCER INCIDENCE:Cancer incidence refers to the occurrence of new cases of cancer in a population and is a key focus of epidemiological studies."}{"title": "CANCER STATISTICS:Cancer statistics provide data on cancer incidence, survival rates, and mortality, which are crucial for public health research."}{"title": "EUR HEART J:Eur Heart J is a journal that publishes research related to cardiovascular disease in Europe."}{"title": "GBD 2013:GBD 2013 refers to the Global Burden of Disease study conducted in 2013, analyzing mortality and causes of death."}{"title": "PREDIMED TRIAL:The PREDIMED trial is a large-scale randomized clinical study designed to assess the effects of the Mediterranean diet on cardiovascular disease and overall cardiovascular health. This trial investigates how adherence to the Mediterranean diet influences various health outcomes related to cardiovascular conditions. Through its comprehensive approach, the PREDIMED trial aims to provide valuable insights into the relationship between diet and cardiovascular health."}{"title": "ESC:The ESC, or European Society of Cardiology, is an organization dedicated to improving cardiovascular health. It is known for issuing comprehensive guidelines that pertain to both the diagnosis and treatment of heart failure, as well as dietary recommendations aimed at promoting heart health. Through its efforts, the ESC plays a crucial role in advancing knowledge and practices related to cardiovascular care."}{"title": "ACC:The American College of Cardiology (ACC) is an organization that develops guidelines for cardiovascular disease management."}{"title": "CHRYSOHOO C:Chrysohoou C is a researcher involved in studies related to the Mediterranean diet and cardiovascular health."}{"title": "DIETARY FACTORS:Dietary factors refer to the various components of diet that can influence health outcomes, particularly in relation to heart disease."}{"title": "HEART VESSELS:Heart Vessels is a medical journal that publishes research related to cardiovascular health and diseases."}{"title": "EUROPEAN JOURNAL OF HEART FAILURE:The European Journal of Heart Failure is a peer-reviewed medical journal focusing on heart failure research and treatment."}{"title": "CIRCULATION CARDIOVASCULAR GENETICS:Circulation Cardiovascular Genetics is a journal that focuses on the genetic aspects of cardiovascular diseases."}{"title": "COSMOS SCREENING STUDY:The COSMOS screening study is a research initiative that examines the health impacts of dietary patterns among heavy smokers."}{"title": "SUDDEN CARDIAC DEATH:Sudden cardiac death is a medical condition that refers to an unexpected death due to cardiac causes, often studied in relation to dietary patterns."}{"title": "DIETARY APPROACHES TO STOP HYPERTENSION:The Dietary Approaches to Stop Hypertension (DASH) is a dietary pattern that emphasizes fruits, vegetables, and low-fat dairy, often compared to the Mediterranean diet in research."}{"title": "CARDIOVASCULAR RISK FACTORS:Cardiovascular risk factors are conditions or behaviors that increase the likelihood of heart disease, often assessed in studies involving dietary patterns."}{"title": "CROSS-SECTIONAL RELATIONSHIP:"}{"title": "TYPE 2 DIABETES MELLITUS:Type 2 diabetes mellitus is a chronic condition that affects the way the body processes blood sugar (glucose) and is often linked to obesity and lifestyle factors."}{"title": "ESPOSITO K:Esposito K is a researcher known for significant contributions to the field of nutrition, particularly through a meta-analysis on the Mediterranean diet. This researcher has been involved in multiple studies examining the effects of the Mediterranean diet on diabetes and cardiovascular health, highlighting its potential benefits in these areas."}{"title": "GIUGLIANO D:Giugliano D is a prominent researcher in the field of nutrition and diabetes, known for his work on the Mediterranean diet."}{"title": "PANAGIOTAKOS D:Panagiotakos D is a researcher who has studied the effects of dietary patterns, including the Mediterranean diet, on health outcomes."}{"title": "SCHWINGSACKL L:Schwingsackl L is a researcher who has conducted systematic reviews and meta-analyses on dietary patterns and health."}{"title": "CESPEDES EM:Cespedes EM is a researcher involved in studies examining dietary patterns and their effects on type 2 diabetes."}{"title": "HUO R:Huo R is a researcher who has contributed to studies on the effects of the Mediterranean diet on glycemic control and cardiovascular risk factors."}{"title": "KOLVEROU E:"}{"title": "HOSPITAL REGIONAL UNIVERSITARIO DE M\u00c1LAGA:The Hospital Regional Universitario de M\u00e1laga is a clinical institution that specializes in various medical treatments, with a particular focus on nutrition and dietetics research. It provides nutrition support for patients suffering from pulmonary diseases, highlighting its commitment to comprehensive patient care. The hospital is staffed by a team of specialists, including Gabriel Olveira Fuster, Victoria Contreras Bol\u00edvar, and Casilda Olveira Fuster, who contribute to its reputation as a leading medical facility in the region."}{"title": "FOOD AND NUTRITION BOARD:The Food and Nutrition Board is a component of the National Academy of Sciences in the United States. It is tasked with the important responsibility of establishing dietary reference intakes, which serve as guidelines for nutritional needs and help inform public health policies and dietary recommendations."}{"title": "INSTITUTO DE MEDICINA:The Instituto de Medicina, also known as the Institute of Medicine (IOM), is a nonprofit organization dedicated to providing expert advice on health and medicine. It is recognized for its role in publishing dietary reference intakes, which include recommendations on daily nutrient intake, such as copper. The organization aims to guide individuals and policymakers in making informed decisions regarding nutrition and health."}{"title": "FEDERACI\u00d3N ESPA\u00d1OLA DE SOCIEDADES DE NUTRICI\u00d3N, ALIMENTACI\u00d3N Y DIET\u00c9TICA:The Spanish Federation of Societies of Nutrition, Food, and Dietetics is an organization that has developed dietary reference intakes for Spain."}{"title": "RECOMMENDED DIETARY ALLOWANCE:The Recommended Dietary Allowance (RDA) is a daily dietary nutrient intake level that is sufficient to meet the requirements of nearly all (97-98%) healthy individuals in a particular life stage and gender group."}{"title": "DIETARY REFERENCE INTAKES:Dietary Reference Intakes (DRI) are a set of reference values designed to plan and assess nutrient intakes for healthy individuals and populations. These guidelines serve to help individuals understand the recommended levels of nutrient intake necessary for maintaining health. The DRI provides a framework for evaluating dietary intake and ensuring that nutritional needs are met, thereby promoting overall well-being."}{"title": "INSTITUTO AMERICANO DE MEDICINA:The American Institute of Medicine provides definitions and guidelines for dietary reference intakes and nutritional requirements."}{"title": "EUROPEAN FEDERATION ASSOCIATION OF HEALTH PRODUCTS MANUFACTURERS:An organization that represents health product manufacturers in Europe, involved in setting nutritional standards."}{"title": "EUROPEAN RESPONSIBLE NUTRITION ALLIANCE:An alliance focused on promoting responsible nutrition practices in Europe."}{"title": "NAP.EDU:A website that provides access to research and publications related to nutrition and health."}{"title": "RIESGO:RIESGO refers to the risk associated with inadequate or excessive nutrient intake as defined in dietary guidelines. Additionally, it encompasses risk management in healthcare, which involves identifying, analyzing, and mitigating potential risks to patient health. This dual focus highlights the importance of both nutritional balance and proactive healthcare strategies in minimizing health-related risks."}{"title": "INGESTA \u00d3PTIMA:The optimal intake levels of nutrients as recommended by health organizations."}{"title": "NIVEL DE INGESTA:The level of nutrient intake that is considered safe or adequate according to dietary guidelines."}{"title": "DRI:Dietary Reference Intakes (DRI) are a set of reference values designed to plan and assess nutrient intakes for healthy individuals. These guidelines encompass recommendations for nutrient intake aimed at promoting health and preventing chronic diseases."}{"title": "RDA:RDA, which stands for Recommended Dietary Allowance, refers to the daily intake levels of essential nutrients that are recommended to maintain health. The RDA represents the average daily level of intake sufficient to meet the nutrient requirements of nearly all (97-98%) healthy individuals. These guidelines are established to prevent nutrient deficiencies and ensure that individuals consume adequate amounts of nutrients necessary for optimal health. In Spanish, RDA is referred to as \"Recomendaciones Diarias de Ingesta,\" emphasizing the importance of these recommendations in daily dietary practices."}{"title": "UL:The Tolerable Upper Intake Level (UL) refers to the maximum daily intake of a nutrient that is unlikely to cause adverse health effects in the general population. This concept is crucial for understanding safe consumption levels of various nutrients, as exceeding the UL may lead to negative health outcomes. The term UL is consistently used to denote these maximum intake levels, emphasizing the importance of adhering to these guidelines to maintain health and prevent toxicity."}{"title": "EAR:The term \"EAR\" stands for Estimated Average Requirement, which is a key measure used in dietary guidelines. It refers to the daily intake value that is estimated to meet the nutritional requirements of half the healthy individuals within a specific life stage and gender group. The Estimated Average Requirements (EAR) represent the average daily nutrient intake levels that are calculated to satisfy the needs of this demographic, ensuring that dietary recommendations are tailored to support the health of various populations effectively."}{"title": "NOAEL:No Observed Adverse Effect Level (NOAEL) is the highest experimental dose that does not cause a significant increase in adverse effects."}{"title": "LOAEL:Lowest Observed Adverse Effect Level (LOAEL) is the lowest experimental dose that causes a significant increase in adverse effects."}{"title": "INGESTA INSUFICIENTE:Insufficient intake refers to the consumption of nutrients below the recommended levels, leading to potential health risks."}{"title": "INGESTA EXCESIVA:Excessive intake refers to the consumption of nutrients above the recommended levels, which can lead to adverse health effects."}{"title": "EFECTOS ADVERSOS:Adverse effects are negative health outcomes resulting from inadequate or excessive nutrient intake."}{"title": "EU:The European Union (EU) is a political and economic union of member states primarily located in Europe. It plays a significant role in regulating food standards, including those specifically for athlete-targeted products. Additionally, the EU provides dietary recommendations for sodium intake and is actively working on harmonizing food labeling legislation across its member states."}{"title": "AI:Adequate Intake (AI) is a recommended intake level based on observed or experimentally determined estimates of nutrient intake by a group of healthy people."}{"title": "NUTRIENT:Nutrients are substances that provide nourishment essential for the maintenance of life and for growth."}{"title": "FOOD LABELING:Food labeling refers to the information provided on food packaging that informs consumers about the nutritional content and ingredients."}{"title": "SENC:SENC, or the Sociedad Espa\u00f1ola de Nutrici\u00f3n Comunitaria, is a scientific organization dedicated to the development of nutritional recommendations and dietary guidelines for the general population. From 2000 to 2016, SENC focused on creating comprehensive nutritional advice, which includes the adaptation of the healthy eating pyramid in 2015. Additionally, SENC places a particular emphasis on providing dietary recommendations for pediatric patients, ensuring that nutritional guidance is tailored to the needs of younger demographics. Overall, SENC plays a crucial role in promoting community nutrition in Spain through its evidence-based guidelines and recommendations."}{"title": "EURODIET:EURODIET is a dietary guideline initiative established in 2000 that aims to provide comprehensive recommendations on nutrition across Europe. The project focuses on creating dietary guidelines that incorporate proposals from various European countries, ensuring that the recommendations are relevant and applicable to diverse populations within the region. Through its efforts, EURODIET seeks to promote better nutritional practices and improve public health across Europe."}{"title": "NAS:The NAS, or National Academy of Sciences, is a private, nonprofit institution comprised of distinguished scholars dedicated to scientific and engineering research. Established to provide expert advice on various scientific and technical issues, the NAS plays a significant role in formulating dietary guidelines. In 2002, the NAS published dietary recommendations that include the definition of the Recommended Dietary Allowance (RDA) for carbohydrates. Additionally, the NAS proposes formulas for calculating estimated energy requirements tailored to different age groups, further contributing to the understanding of nutritional needs across the lifespan."}{"title": "POBLACI\u00d3N GENERAL:The general population refers to the collective group of individuals for whom the nutritional recommendations are intended."}{"title": "EJERCICIO:EJERCICIO refers to any bodily movement that consumes energy, which is essential for health and the performance of athletes. It encompasses physical activity that is planned, structured, and repetitive, aimed at improving or maintaining physical fitness. This dual perspective highlights the importance of exercise not only as a means of enhancing athletic performance but also as a crucial component of overall well-being."}{"title": "REQUERIMIENTOS ENERG\u00c9TICOS:\"REQUERIMIENTOS ENERG\u00c9TICOS\" refers to the dietary intake of energy necessary to maintain energy balance in healthy individuals. This concept encompasses the caloric needs for both adults and children, with specific guidelines tailored to different age groups and activity levels. For adults, energy requirements are focused on maintaining overall health, while for children, these requirements are adjusted according to their developmental needs and physical activity."}{"title": "EFECTO TERMOG\u00c9NICO DE LOS ALIMENTOS:The thermic effect of food refers to the increase in metabolic rate after ingestion of a meal, accounting for approximately 10% of total energy consumed."}{"title": "NIVELES DE ACTIVIDAD F\u00cdSICA:Physical activity levels are defined as the ratio of total energy expenditure to basal energy expenditure, indicating the level of physical activity of an individual."}{"title": "PAL:PAL, which stands for Physical Activity Level, is a measure utilized to categorize energy requirements based on the intensity of physical activity. It serves as an assessment tool for evaluating an individual's energy expenditure in relation to their activity level."}{"title": "NATIONAL ACADEMY OF SCIENCES:The National Academy of Sciences (NAS) is a United States nonprofit organization dedicated to providing expert advice on scientific and technical issues. It serves as a private, non-profit society composed of distinguished scholars who are actively engaged in scientific and engineering research. In addition to offering guidance on a wide range of scientific matters, the NAS conducts studies specifically related to health and nutrition, further emphasizing its commitment to addressing critical scientific challenges and informing public policy."}{"title": "WOMEN:Women are a demographic group referenced in dietary guidelines, which often include specific nutritional recommendations tailored to their needs. Additionally, in a particular study involving women, some participants faced challenges in performing the grip strength test due to difficulties with the dynamometer. This highlights the importance of considering the unique circumstances and requirements of women in both nutritional and physical assessments."}{"title": "SUGARS:Sugars are a type of carbohydrate that should be limited in the diet according to health guidelines."}{"title": "PHYSICAL ACTIVITY:Physical activity refers to bodily movement that expends energy and plays a crucial role in overall health. It has been observed that physical activity levels have decreased in the population, contributing to rising obesity rates. Additionally, physical activity is a significant lifestyle factor that influences the prevalence and progression of conditions such as sarcopenia and frailty. Health guidelines recommend a minimum amount of daily exercise to promote well-being and mitigate these health issues. Overall, engaging in regular physical activity is essential for maintaining a healthy lifestyle and preventing various health complications."}{"title": "SOCIETY OF SPANISH COMMUNITY NUTRITION:The Sociedad Espa\u00f1ola de Nutrici\u00f3n Comunitaria (SENC) is an organization focused on community nutrition in Spain."}{"title": "\u00c1CIDOS GRASOS SATURADOS:\u00c1CIDOS GRASOS SATURADOS, or saturated fatty acids, are a type of fat that can significantly impact cholesterol levels and are often compared to unsaturated fats in dietary studies. These fats are typically recommended to be limited in a healthy diet due to their association with cardiovascular health. It is particularly important to restrict the intake of saturated fatty acids in children's diets to promote heart health. Additionally, \u00c1CIDOS GRASOS SATURADOS are included in nutritional information and are frequently evaluated in dietary research for their effects on health."}{"title": "APORTES DIET\u00c9TICOS RECOMENDADOS:Dietary Reference Intakes (DRIs) are a set of reference values used to plan and assess nutrient intakes."}{"title": "RECOMENDACIONES DE 2015 SOBRE AZ\u00daCARES:The 2015 recommendations on sugar intake provide guidelines for adults and children regarding sugar consumption."}{"title": "INGESTA ADECUADA:INGESTA ADECUADA refers to the recommended intake levels of various nutrients, specifically tailored for children. This concept encompasses adequate intake, which is defined as a recommended intake level of a nutrient based on observed or experimentally determined estimates of nutrient intake by a group of healthy individuals. Thus, INGESTA ADECUADA serves as a guideline to ensure that children receive the necessary nutrients for their growth and development, based on established dietary recommendations."}{"title": "FIBRA TOTAL:Total fiber is the sum of dietary fiber and functional fiber, which is important for digestive health."}{"title": "INGESTA DE EPA + DHA:The intake of EPA (Eicosapentaenoic acid) and DHA (Docosahexaenoic acid) is recommended for cardiovascular health."}{"title": "NUTRICI\u00d3N INTERACTIVA:NUTRICI\u00d3N INTERACTIVA is an interactive platform developed by the Society of Spanish Endocrinology and Nutrition (SEEN) aimed at promoting nutrition education and awareness. This web platform serves as a valuable resource for online nutritional calculations, providing users with tools to estimate energy requirements and assess nutritional needs. Through its comprehensive offerings, NUTRICI\u00d3N INTERACTIVA seeks to enhance understanding of nutrition and support individuals in making informed dietary choices."}{"title": "GEB:GEB, or Gasto Energ\u00e9tico Basal, refers to the basal energy expenditure, which is the measure of the energy required by the body at rest to maintain essential physiological functions. This concept is crucial for estimating energy needs and is calculated based on factors such as weight and height, particularly for children. GEB serves as a fundamental metric in understanding the energy requirements of individuals, highlighting its importance in both health and nutrition contexts."}{"title": "GER:GER, which stands for Gasto Energ\u00e9tico en Reposo, is a measure of resting energy expenditure that is particularly important for dietary management in patients with cystic fibrosis. It is also referred to as Gasto Energ\u00e9tico de Reposo, highlighting its relevance to energy expenditure in individuals. This metric plays a crucial role in understanding and managing the energy needs of those affected by cystic fibrosis."}{"title": "GET:Gasto Energ\u00e9tico Total (GET) refers to the total energy expenditure, which is calculated based on physical activity."}{"title": "RANGOS ACEPTABLES DE DISTRIBUCI\u00d3N DE NUTRIENTES:Acceptable Macronutrient Distribution Ranges (AMDR) are guidelines for nutrient intake to reduce chronic disease risk."}{"title": "AGCML N-3:AGCML n-3 refers to high supplements of omega-3 fatty acids that may increase lipid peroxidation and reduce cytokine production."}{"title": "CITOQUINAS:Citoquinas, also known as cytokines, are crucial signaling molecules that mediate and regulate various biological processes, including immunity, inflammation, and hematopoiesis. They play a significant role in the immune response, acting as inflammatory mediators that can be influenced by dietary intake. In patients with renal issues, dietary adjustments can help reduce the levels of cytokines, highlighting their relevance in managing inflammation and immune responses.\n\nCitoquinas are released by cells and are involved in metabolic inflammation, making them important in various health conditions, including chronic pancreatitis. During sepsis, inflammatory cytokines can be released, potentially affecting liver function and leading to hepatobiliary complications. Additionally, elevated levels of citoquinas have been observed in patients with chronic liver disease, where they are associated with anorexia and malnutrition. These proteins can also interfere with protein synthesis, which may impact the effectiveness of artificial nutrition in advanced patients.\n\nOverall, citoquinas are essential proteins in cell signaling, particularly in the context of immune responses and inflammation, and their regulation is vital for maintaining health and managing various medical conditions."}{"title": "INGESTA DE TOCOFEROL:Tocopherol intake is related to the dietary consumption of vitamin E, which can influence lipid peroxidation."}{"title": "POBLACIONES MADURAS:Older populations, particularly those over 50 years of age, are discussed in the context of health risks and dietary recommendations."}{"title": "ENERG\u00cdA TOTAL:Total energy expenditure (GET) is calculated based on basal metabolic rate and physical activity levels."}{"title": "C. M\u00c9TODO 3:A method described for estimating energy expenditure based on activity levels and time spent on various activities."}{"title": "ALIMENTACION:Refers to dietary practices and their impact on health, particularly in relation to energy expenditure and weight management."}{"title": "REPOSO:Refers to the activity of resting or sleeping, which is associated with a specific energy expenditure factor."}{"title": "MUY LIGERA:Refers to very light activities such as painting or writing, which have a specific energy expenditure factor."}{"title": "LIGERA:Refers to light activities like walking or cleaning, which have a specific energy expenditure factor."}{"title": "MODERADA:Refers to moderate activities such as cycling or dancing, which have a specific energy expenditure factor."}{"title": "INTENSA:Refers to intense activities like football or climbing, which have a specific energy expenditure factor."}{"title": "ESTILO DE VIDA SEDENTARIA:Refers to a sedentary lifestyle characterized by low physical activity, impacting energy expenditure."}{"title": "ESTILO DE VIDA ACTIVO:Refers to an active lifestyle with moderate physical activity, impacting energy expenditure."}{"title": "ESTILO DE VIDA MUY INTENSA:Refers to a very intense lifestyle with high physical activity, impacting energy expenditure."}{"title": "VARONES:The entity \"VARONES\" refers to a demographic group of males, which, despite being less studied than their female counterparts, also faces a significant risk of developing eating disorders, with a prevalence ratio of 9:1 compared to women. This group is categorized by age for health and demographic statistics, specifically including males aged 19-30 years, 31-50 years, 51-70 years, and those over 70 years. Additionally, males aged 20 years and older are considered for dietary intake recommendations. The data also indicates that these males participated in a study focused on measuring grip strength, highlighting their involvement in health-related assessments. Overall, \"VARONES\" encompasses a diverse range of males with varying health metrics and dietary needs, underscoring the importance of addressing their specific health risks and requirements."}{"title": "TAREAS DOM\u00c9STICAS NO MECANIZADAS:Domestic tasks performed manually without machinery, such as sweeping, washing clothes, and washing dishes, which also require physical effort."}{"title": "ACTIVIDADES L\u00daDICAS:Leisure activities that include light physical exertion, such as watching TV or using a computer."}{"title": "DORMIR:The act of sleeping, which is essential for recovery and energy conservation."}{"title": "ASEO PERSONAL:Personal hygiene activities, including dressing and showering, which require a certain amount of physical activity."}{"title": "COMER:The act of eating, which is a necessary daily activity for energy intake."}{"title": "COCINAR:The act of preparing food, which involves physical activity and energy expenditure."}{"title": "RECOGER AGUA O MADERA:Activities that involve collecting water or firewood, which require physical effort and are part of daily chores."}{"title": "CAMINAR:Walking at different paces without carrying weight, which is a form of physical activity."}{"title": "AGRICULTURA NO MECANIZADA:"}{"title": "AGENCIA ESPA\u00d1OLA DE CONSUMO, SEGURIDAD ALIMENTARIA Y NUTRICI\u00d3N:The AGENCIA ESPA\u00d1OLA DE CONSUMO, SEGURIDAD ALIMENTARIA Y NUTRICI\u00d3N, also known as the Spanish Agency for Consumer Affairs, Food Safety and Nutrition (AECOSAN), is tasked with the critical role of ensuring food safety and consumer protection throughout Spain. This agency is dedicated to safeguarding the health and rights of consumers by overseeing food safety standards and implementing regulations that protect public health."}{"title": "ACIDOS GRASOS TRANS:ACIDOS GRASOS TRANS, or trans fatty acids, are a type of unsaturated fat that have been linked to several health risks, notably cardiovascular disease and diabetes. These unhealthy fats are particularly detrimental for individuals with diabetes, as they can negatively impact cholesterol levels. It is recommended that trans fatty acids be avoided in the diet to promote better health outcomes."}{"title": "MORTALIDAD TOTAL:MORTALIDAD TOTAL refers to the overall death rate within a population. This metric can be influenced by various factors, including dietary habits and health conditions, which play a significant role in determining the mortality outcomes in a given demographic."}{"title": "FESNAD:FESNAD, or the Spanish Federation of Nutrition and Dietetics, is an organization dedicated to promoting nutrition and dietary practices in Spain. It provides dietary reference intakes specifically tailored for the Spanish population, ensuring that nutritional guidelines are relevant and applicable to local dietary habits. Additionally, FESNAD plays a crucial role in establishing guidelines on the consumption of fats and oils in the diet, particularly for the adult Spanish population. This initiative is encapsulated in the Spanish Consensus on Fats and Oils in the Diet, which is actively promoted by FESNAD to enhance public understanding and adherence to healthy dietary practices."}{"title": "GEPREM-HG:GEPREM-Hg refers to a study group dedicated to the prevention of methylmercury exposure in the Spanish population. This group has developed recommendations regarding fish consumption, which are based on the tolerable weekly intake of methylmercury established by the European Food Safety Authority (EFSA). GEPREM-Hg has created a consensus document that outlines specific consumption recommendations tailored to various factors such as age, weight, type of fish, and the possibility of pregnancy, aiming to minimize the risks associated with methylmercury exposure."}{"title": "USDA:The United States Department of Agriculture (USDA) is a government agency that plays a crucial role in promoting public health through its dietary guidelines for Americans. These guidelines include specific recommendations on cholesterol consumption, aiming to educate the public on healthy eating habits. Additionally, the USDA provides a comprehensive database of food composition and dietary surveys, which serves as a valuable resource for understanding nutritional data. To further assist families in making healthy food choices, the USDA created the \"My Plate\" nutritional guide, which is designed to help parents feed their children nutritious meals. Overall, the USDA is dedicated to enhancing the nutritional well-being of the American population through its various initiatives and resources."}{"title": "METILMERCURIO:Methylmercury is a contaminant commonly found in fish, recognized for its potential adverse health effects. It is a toxic compound that poses significant risks, especially to vulnerable populations such as pregnant women and young children. Due to these health concerns, there are specific consumption recommendations in place to mitigate exposure to methylmercury."}{"title": "COLESTEROL DIET\u00c9TICO:Colesterol diet\u00e9tico refers to dietary cholesterol obtained from animal foods, which plays a role in cardiovascular health. While it is a nutrient that can impact health, both the American Heart Association and the USDA suggest that dietary cholesterol does not require restriction in a healthy diet. This indicates that, for most individuals, moderate consumption of dietary cholesterol from animal sources can be part of a balanced diet without significant health risks."}{"title": "\u00c1CIDOS GRASOS TRANS:\u00c1CIDOS GRASOS TRANS, or trans fatty acids, are a type of fatty acid characterized by their strong positive effect on both atherogenesis and thrombogenesis. These fats are isomers derived from unsaturated fatty acids, primarily produced during the hydrogenation process, which is commonly used in the production of margarine. Due to their adverse effects on cardiovascular health, nutritional guidelines recommend limiting the intake of trans fatty acids in the diet. Furthermore, it is particularly important to restrict these unhealthy fats in children's diets to prevent potential health issues."}{"title": "SUGAR:Sugar refers to sweet, short-chain carbohydrates that are used in food and beverages, with guidelines suggesting limits on their intake for health reasons."}{"title": "CAVITIES:Cavities, or dental caries, are a common dental problem that can be exacerbated by high sugar intake."}{"title": "METHYLMERCURY:"}{"title": "AZ\u00daCARES LIBRES:The consumption of free sugars is associated with dental caries, particularly when it exceeds 10% of total energy intake."}{"title": "ALIMENTOS RICOS EN FIBRA:Foods high in fiber, especially fruits and vegetables, are associated with a probable decrease in the risk of several diseases."}{"title": "CARIES DENTAL:"}{"title": "ALCOHOL CONSUMPTION:Alcohol consumption, especially in chronic cases, is a significant lifestyle factor that can contribute to the development of osteoporosis. Additionally, the event of alcohol consumption is associated with various health risks and has implications for mortality. These effects highlight the importance of understanding the impact of alcohol consumption on overall health and well-being."}{"title": "SODIUM INTAKE:The event of sodium intake recommendations is discussed, particularly in relation to hypertension."}{"title": "POTASSIUM INTAKE:The event of potassium intake recommendations is discussed, emphasizing its role in reducing blood pressure."}{"title": "VEGETARIAN DIET:The vegetarian diet is a dietary pattern that emphasizes the consumption of fruits, vegetables, whole grains, legumes, seeds, and nuts. It may also include dairy and eggs, depending on the specific type of vegetarianism practiced. This diet has been extensively studied for its association with cardiovascular disease risk factors and is linked to various health benefits. Additionally, the vegetarian diet is relevant in discussions about protein quality and dietary recommendations tailored for individuals with diverse eating habits. Overall, the vegetarian diet is recognized for its potential to promote health and well-being."}{"title": "VEGETALES:Los vegetales son fuentes naturales de nutrientes esenciales, incluyendo \u00e1cido f\u00f3lico y vitamina C, que son importantes para la salud general."}{"title": "DIETAS VEGETARIANAS:\"DIETAS VEGETARIANAS\" refers to dietary patterns that predominantly exclude meat. These diets can be beneficial for health, particularly for individuals with diabetes, when they are well-planned. However, it is important for those following vegetarian diets to pay special attention to their intake of certain nutrients, such as vitamin B12 and iron, to ensure they meet their nutritional needs."}{"title": "SUPLEMENTOS:Los suplementos, que incluyen hierro, \u00e1cido f\u00f3lico, calcio y vitaminas, son productos esenciales utilizados para aumentar la ingesta de nutrientes necesarios, especialmente en pacientes con POIC (P\u00e9rdida \u00d3sea Inducida por C\u00e1ncer) y en poblaciones con dietas restrictivas o deficiencias confirmadas. Estos suplementos son fundamentales para prevenir deficiencias nutricionales y asegurar una adecuada salud y bienestar en estos grupos vulnerables."}{"title": "MUJERES EMBARAZADAS:Mujeres embarazadas are pregnant women who undergo monitoring for anemia, a condition that can affect their health and the health of their unborn child. During pregnancy, these women may require iron supplementation to address any deficiencies and ensure a healthy pregnancy."}{"title": "SOCIETY OF DIETETICS AND FOOD SCIENCE:The Society of Dietetics and Food Science is an organization that provides guidelines and information on nutrition and dietary practices."}{"title": "MEDITERRANEAN DIET PYRAMID:The Mediterranean Diet Pyramid is a visual representation of dietary recommendations emphasizing fruits, vegetables, and healthy fats."}{"title": "CHOOSE MY PLATE:Choose My Plate is a dietary guideline initiative by the United States Department of Agriculture aimed at promoting healthy eating habits."}{"title": "FOOD PYRAMID:The Food Pyramid is a graphical representation of dietary guidelines that categorizes food into different groups to promote balanced eating."}{"title": "FOOD GUIDE WHEEL:The Food Guide Wheel is a circular representation of food groups aimed at educating the public about healthy eating."}{"title": "VITAMIN D SUPPLEMENTATION:Vitamin D supplementation involves taking vitamin D in supplement form, particularly for populations at risk of deficiency, such as older adults."}{"title": "DIETARY COMPONENTS:Dietary components include various biologically active factors in foods, such as flavonoids and carotenoids, that may influence health outcomes."}{"title": "HEALTHY DIET PATTERNS:Healthy diet patterns, such as the Mediterranean diet, emphasize the consumption of fruits, vegetables, and healthy fats to reduce chronic disease risk."}{"title": "NUTRITIONAL DEFICIENCIES:Nutritional deficiencies are health issues that arise from the inadequate intake or absorption of essential nutrients. These deficiencies can lead to various health problems and are often associated with conditions such as celiac disease. The body requires a sufficient amount of essential nutrients to function properly, and when these nutrients are lacking, it can result in significant health complications. Nutritional guidelines are designed to help prevent these deficiencies by promoting adequate nutrient intake."}{"title": "CALCIUM SUPPLEMENTATION:"}{"title": "EUROPEAN UNION:The European Union is a political and economic union comprising 27 member states primarily located in Europe. It plays a significant role in regulating various standards, including those related to organic product labeling, among other areas."}{"title": "NATIONAL ACADEMY PRESS:The National Academy Press is a publishing entity that specializes in producing reports and books on a wide range of topics, with a particular focus on health and nutrition. This includes the publication of materials related to dietary reference intakes, among other subjects. Through its publications, the National Academy Press aims to disseminate valuable information and research findings to inform and educate the public and professionals in the field."}{"title": "BANGKOK:Bangkok is the capital city of Thailand, where a joint FAO/WHO expert consultation took place."}{"title": "GENEVA:Geneva is a city in Switzerland that serves as a global hub for diplomacy and international organizations, including the World Health Organization (WHO). The city is notable for hosting consultations and publishing guidelines on nutrition, reflecting its significant role in international health discussions and initiatives."}{"title": "JAKICIC JM:Jakicic JM is a researcher involved in the 2013 AHA/ACC guideline on lifestyle management to reduce cardiovascular risk."}{"title": "ARD JD:Ard JD is a contributor to the 2013 AHA/ACC guideline on lifestyle management to reduce cardiovascular risk."}{"title": "DE JESUS JM:De Jesus JM is a researcher who worked on the 2013 AHA/ACC guideline on lifestyle management to reduce cardiovascular risk."}{"title": "HOUSTON MILLER N:Houston Miller N is a researcher involved in the 2013 AHA/ACC guideline on lifestyle management to reduce cardiovascular risk."}{"title": "HUBBARD VS:Hubbard VS is a contributor to the 2013 AHA/ACC guideline on lifestyle management to reduce cardiovascular risk."}{"title": "NATIONAL ACADEMIES PRESS:The National Academies Press is a prominent publisher that specializes in producing reports and guidelines on a wide range of topics, particularly focusing on health and nutrition. It is known for its publications related to dietary reference intakes for macronutrients and other scientific subjects. The reports and books published by the National Academies Press are issued by the National Academies of Sciences, Engineering, and Medicine, and they provide expert advice and insights on various health-related issues."}{"title": "FAO FOOD NUTR PAP:FAO Food Nutr Pap is a publication that includes reports on food and nutrition topics."}{"title": "EUROPEAN FOOD SAFETY AUTHORITY:The European Food Safety Authority (EFSA) is an agency that plays a crucial role in evaluating scientific evidence related to food safety and nutrition within the European Union. It provides independent scientific advice on food-related risks, including the assessment of food additives and the establishment of acceptable daily intake levels. EFSA is also involved in communicating both existing and emerging food safety issues to ensure public health. Notably, the agency has conducted studies on the effects of creatine supplementation on muscle strength, particularly in older adults, and has examined the relationship between creatine and resistance training. Through its comprehensive evaluations and guidance, EFSA aims to safeguard food safety and promote informed decision-making regarding nutrition in the EU."}{"title": "SOCIEDAD ESPA\u00d1OLA DE NUTRICI\u00d3N COMUNITARIA:The Sociedad Espa\u00f1ola de Nutrici\u00f3n Comunitaria is an organization focused on community nutrition in Spain, known for publishing dietary guidelines for the Spanish population."}{"title": "PREDIMED STUDY:The PREDIMED Study, which stands for PREvenci\u00f3n con DIeta MEDiterr\u00e1nea, is a comprehensive research initiative aimed at the primary prevention of cardiovascular disease through the adoption of a Mediterranean diet. This study investigates the various benefits of the Mediterranean diet on cardiovascular health, focusing on its effects on mortality, particularly in populations with high fish consumption. Additionally, the PREDIMED Study examines the impact of dietary alpha-linolenic acid and marine omega-3 fatty acids, further contributing to the understanding of how specific dietary components can influence cardiovascular outcomes. Overall, the PREDIMED Study plays a crucial role in exploring the relationship between diet and heart health, emphasizing the importance of the Mediterranean dietary pattern."}{"title": "AGENCIA ESPA\u00d1OLA DE CONSUMO SEGURIDAD ALIMENTARIA Y NUTRICI\u00d3N:The Spanish Agency for Consumer Affairs, Food Safety and Nutrition is responsible for ensuring food safety and promoting healthy eating habits in Spain."}{"title": "ALIMENTOS EN ESPA\u00d1A 2015:A report detailing the content of trans fatty acids in foods available in Spain in 2015."}{"title": "SUGARS INTAKE GUIDELINE:A guideline published by WHO regarding the recommended intake of sugars for adults and children."}{"title": "CARBOHYDRATES IN HUMAN NUTRITION:A scientific update by FAO/WHO on the role of carbohydrates in human nutrition."}{"title": "DIETARY FAT INTAKE STUDY:A study examining the relationship between dietary fat intake and cardiovascular disease risk."}{"title": "NUTRICI\u00d3N EN EL ADULTO:"}{"title": "INTERNATIONAL CARBOHYDRATE QUALITY CONSORTIUM:The International Carbohydrate Quality Consortium (ICQC) is an organization that focuses on scientific consensus regarding carbohydrate quality and its impact on health."}{"title": "BEYOND AGEING PROJECT:The Beyond Ageing Project is a randomized controlled trial aimed at preventing cognitive decline in older adults through supplementation of folic acid and vitamin B-12."}{"title": "COMPLEJO HOSPITALARIO UNIVERSITARIO DE FERROL:The Complejo Hospitalario Universitario de Ferrol is a healthcare facility situated in A Coru\u00f1a, Spain. It offers a range of medical services, with a particular focus on endocrinology and nutrition. This institution is recognized for its commitment to providing comprehensive healthcare to the community, ensuring access to specialized medical care in these important fields."}{"title": "CARDIOVASCULAR DISEASES:Cardiovascular diseases refer to a group of disorders affecting the heart and blood vessels, often influenced by diet and nutrition."}{"title": "NUTRITIONAL LABELING:Nutritional labeling refers to the practice of providing information about the nutritional content of food products to help consumers make informed choices. This includes details about various dietary attributes, such as gluten content, enabling individuals to better understand the nutritional value and ingredients of the foods they consume."}{"title": "CONSUMO ALIMENTARIO:Consumo alimentario refers to the act of consuming food, which is linked to health and the preparation of meals at home."}{"title": "ETIQUETADO NUTRICIONAL:The entity \"ETIQUETADO NUTRICIONAL\" refers to nutritional labeling, which encompasses the regulations and information presented on food packaging. This labeling is designed to inform consumers about the nutritional content of food products, helping them make informed dietary choices."}{"title": "REGLAMENTO (UE) N\u00ba 1169/2011:Reglamento (UE) N\u00ba 1169/2011 is a legal framework established by the European Parliament and Council that governs the information related to food that must be provided to consumers. This regulation aims to ensure that consumers receive clear and accurate information about the food products they purchase, thereby promoting informed choices and enhancing food safety."}{"title": "ALIMENTOS ENVASADOS:Packaged foods are those that are sealed before sale, requiring clear labeling of their contents."}{"title": "PRODUCTOS ALIMENTARIOS:Food products are items that are consumed and require clear labeling to inform consumers about their nutritional content."}{"title": "ETIQUETADO:ETIQUETADO refers to the labeling process that encompasses the information required to be present on food products, particularly those with very low caloric content, as mandated by regulations. This includes adherence to specific norms that govern the information displayed on food items, especially concerning allergens. Additionally, ETIQUETADO involves providing essential details such as the minimum durability date and nutritional information, which aids consumers in understanding the contents and nutritional value of the food they purchase. Overall, ETIQUETADO plays a crucial role in ensuring transparency and safety in food labeling."}{"title": "REAL DECRETO 1245/2008:El Real Decreto 1245/2008 es una legislaci\u00f3n espa\u00f1ola que regula la informaci\u00f3n sobre los aditivos alimentarios y su etiquetado."}{"title": "EMPRESA ALIMENTARIA:La empresa alimentaria es la entidad responsable de la producci\u00f3n y etiquetado de productos alimenticios, incluyendo la informaci\u00f3n sobre ingredientes y al\u00e9rgenos."}{"title": "CONSUMIDORES:Los consumidores son las personas que compran y consumen productos alimenticios, y tienen derecho a recibir informaci\u00f3n clara sobre los mismos."}{"title": "PRODUCTOS ALIMENTICIOS:Los productos alimenticios son bienes que se consumen y que deben cumplir con regulaciones espec\u00edficas sobre etiquetado y seguridad alimentaria."}{"title": "MANTEQUILLA:MANTEQUILLA, commonly known as butter, is a dairy product derived from the fat and protein components of milk. It is characterized by its composition, which includes 50.5% saturated fats, 23.4% monounsaturated fats, and 3.1% polyunsaturated fats. While butter can enhance the flavor of meals and is often used in cooking and as a spread, it is important to consume it in moderation according to dietary guidelines. \n\nMANTEQUILLA is included in various dietary plans, but it is not permitted in modified diets, particularly those that are strict or low-sodium. Additionally, it is noted that butter can contain lactose, which may pose issues for individuals with lactose intolerance; however, it is also mentioned that butter can be lactose-free due to the separation of its aqueous and fatty components during production. \n\nFurthermore, clear labeling regarding ingredients and potential allergens is essential for MANTEQUILLA, especially in children's diets, where it should be consumed occasionally and in moderation. Overall, MANTEQUILLA is a versatile dairy product that plays a role in culinary applications while requiring careful consideration in dietary contexts."}{"title": "NATA FERMENTADA:La nata fermentada es un producto l\u00e1cteo que debe cumplir con las regulaciones de etiquetado de la Uni\u00f3n Europea."}{"title": "ORGANISMOS MODIFICADOS GEN\u00c9TICAMENTE:Los organismos modificados gen\u00e9ticamente (OMG) son productos que deben ser claramente indicados en las etiquetas si su presencia supera el 0,5%."}{"title": "FECHAS DE DURACI\u00d3N/CADUCIDAD:Las fechas de duraci\u00f3n y caducidad son informaci\u00f3n cr\u00edtica que debe aparecer en el etiquetado de productos alimenticios para garantizar la seguridad del consumidor."}{"title": "CANTIDAD NETA:La cantidad neta es la medida del contenido de un producto alimenticio que debe ser claramente indicada en su etiquetado."}{"title": "INFORMACI\u00d3N NUTRICIONAL:La informaci\u00f3n nutricional incluye datos sobre el valor energ\u00e9tico y la composici\u00f3n de los productos alimenticios, y debe ser presentada en las etiquetas."}{"title": "VINAGRES DE FERMENTACI\u00d3N:"}{"title": "REGLEMENTO 1169/2011:El Reglamento 1169/2011 establece normas sobre la informaci\u00f3n alimentaria proporcionada a los consumidores, incluyendo etiquetado y presentaci\u00f3n de informaci\u00f3n nutricional."}{"title": "GALLETAS MARIA:Galletas Maria es un producto alimenticio que contiene varios ingredientes, incluyendo harina de trigo y grasas vegetales."}{"title": "BARES:Los bares son establecimientos que sirven comidas y bebidas, donde se requiere informaci\u00f3n obligatoria sobre los alimentos no envasados."}{"title": "RESTAURANTES:Los restaurantes son lugares que ofrecen comidas y deben cumplir con la normativa de informaci\u00f3n alimentaria."}{"title": "COLEGIOS:Los colegios son instituciones educativas que tambi\u00e9n deben informar sobre los alimentos que sirven a los estudiantes."}{"title": "HORTALIZAS:Las hortalizas son productos frescos que se comercializan sin envasar y deben cumplir con la normativa de etiquetado. Se consideran vegetales que deben ser consumidos en porciones diarias, y se recomienda evitar las hortalizas congeladas que contengan cremas o bechamel."}{"title": "ANTIOXIDANTES E-306, E-304:Los antioxidantes E-306 y E-304 son aditivos alimentarios utilizados en productos como las galletas para preservar su frescura."}{"title": "SUSTANCIAS QUE CAUSAN ALERGIAS:Las sustancias que causan alergias son ingredientes que deben ser claramente informados en los productos alimenticios."}{"title": "MIEL:MIEL, or honey, is a natural sweetener produced by bees. It is a sweet substance that is commonly used in various foods and beverages. As a product, MIEL must adhere to specific labeling regulations and provide clear information to consumers. It is important to note that honey is not recommended for infants under 12 months due to the risk of botulism, a serious illness caused by toxins produced by bacteria that can be present in honey."}{"title": "PRODUCTOS NO ENVASADOS:Los productos no envasados son aquellos que se presentan sin envasar y requieren informaci\u00f3n obligatoria sobre su contenido."}{"title": "INGREDIENTES:Los ingredientes son componentes esenciales de los productos alimenticios que deben ser listados y etiquetados de acuerdo con las regulaciones. Estos ingredientes son utilizados en la elaboraci\u00f3n de productos alimenticios y deben cumplir con normativas espec\u00edficas para garantizar la seguridad y calidad de los alimentos."}{"title": "GALLETA MARIA:Galleta Maria is a type of biscuit made primarily from wheat flour, sugar, and palm fat, with various nutritional components and ingredients listed for consumer information."}{"title": "TRIGO:TRIGO, or wheat, is a cereal grain that is widely consumed around the world and serves as a primary source of gluten. It is important to note that wheat must be excluded from the diets of patients with celiac disease due to its gluten content. Additionally, wheat can contain fructans, which may lead to symptoms in individuals who are sensitive to FODMAPs. In culinary applications, wheat is a key ingredient in products such as Galleta Maria, where it contributes to both the structure and nutritional value of the food. Furthermore, wheat is recognized as a major source of fructans in Western diets, playing a significant role in the intake of these carbohydrates."}{"title": "PALMA:Palma refers to palm fat, an ingredient in Galleta Maria that contributes to its texture and flavor."}{"title": "NUTRICIONAL INFORMACI\u00d3N:Nutritional information is a mandatory disclosure for food products, detailing energy value and nutrient content, which is essential for consumer awareness."}{"title": "COMPOSICI\u00d3N NUTRICIONAL:Composici\u00f3n nutricional refers to the detailed breakdown of nutrients in Galleta Maria, including calories, fats, carbohydrates, and proteins."}{"title": "FRUCTOSA:FRUCTOSA, also known as fructose, is a simple sugar that is naturally found in many fruits and plants, contributing to their sweetness. It is sweeter than glucose and is often used in various food products, which can lead to increased consumption. While FRUCTOSA is absorbed more slowly than glucose, it can significantly affect uric acid metabolism, potentially leading to increased levels of hyperuricemia. \n\nIn dietary contexts, FRUCTOSA is important to consider for individuals managing diabetes, as it can affect blood sugar levels. It is also noted that FRUCTOSA does not alleviate hypoglycemia in individuals with glycogen storage disease type I and may worsen acidosis. Additionally, some individuals may experience hereditary intolerance to FRUCTOSA due to a lack of the enzyme necessary for its metabolism, which can result in gastrointestinal symptoms similar to lactose malabsorption.\n\nFRUCTOSA is included in products like Galleta Maria, enhancing their flavor profile. However, its consumption should be moderated, especially in children with glycogen storage disease type I, as excessive intake can lead to malabsorption issues and gastrointestinal discomfort. Overall, while FRUCTOSA is a common and naturally occurring sugar, its effects on health and metabolism warrant careful consideration in dietary practices."}{"title": "TABLA 3:\"Tabla 3\" serves as a comprehensive resource that encompasses various aspects of nutrition and dietary assessment. It outlines the reference intake of vitamins and minerals for adults, providing essential guidelines for nutritional adequacy. Additionally, it presents commercial combinations of nitrogen and glucose solutions specifically designed for hypocaloric peripheral parenteral nutrition, which is crucial for patients requiring specialized dietary support.\n\nFurthermore, \"Tabla 3\" includes a nutritional assessment based on weight loss percentages over time, allowing for the evaluation of dietary effectiveness and health outcomes. It also details the content of phenylalanine in various foods per 100 grams, which is particularly relevant for individuals managing specific dietary restrictions.\n\nThe table features data from a population study focusing on body mass index (IMC) among men and women aged 45 to 60 years, contributing to a better understanding of nutritional status within this demographic. In addition, \"Tabla 3\" outlines clinical parameters for monitoring patients receiving parenteral nutrition, ensuring that healthcare providers can effectively track patient progress and nutritional needs.\n\nMoreover, it highlights the main problems encountered when analyzing dietary intake records, which is vital for improving dietary assessments and interventions. Lastly, \"Tabla 3\" addresses the negative aspects that powdered ingredients may exhibit when in contact with water, emphasizing the importance of formulation stability in nutritional products. Overall, \"Tabla 3\" is a multifaceted tool that integrates various nutritional data and considerations for both clinical and dietary applications."}{"title": "GRASAS POLIINSATURADAS:Grasas poliinsaturadas are a type of fat that can be included in optional nutritional information."}{"title": "POLIALCOHOLES:Polialcoholes are a type of carbohydrate that can be included in optional nutritional information."}{"title": "FIBRA ALIMENTARIA:FIBRA ALIMENTARIA refers to dietary fiber that can be included in optional nutritional information. It plays a significant role in nutrition, contributing to various health benefits associated with a balanced diet."}{"title": "VALOR ENERG\u00c9TICO:VALOR ENERG\u00c9TICO refers to the energy value provided by food, which is measured in kilojoules or kilocalories. This term encompasses the amount of energy that food supplies to the body, highlighting its importance in nutrition and dietary considerations. The energy value is expressed in both kilojoules and kilocalories, providing a standardized way to quantify the energy content of various food items."}{"title": "GRASAS TOTALES:Grasas totales refer to the total fat content in food, which is part of the nutritional information."}{"title": "AZ\u00daCARES:Az\u00facares, a type of carbohydrate, are included in nutritional information and are categorized as simple carbohydrates. They provide energy but are advised to be limited in dietary guidelines to reduce cardiovascular risk."}{"title": "GRASAS MONOINSATURADAS:"}{"title": "REGULAMENTO 1924/2006:Regulation 1924/2006 governs nutritional claims and health properties of food labeling and advertising."}{"title": "INGESTA DE REFERENCIA:Reference intake is a guideline for the daily amount of energy and nutrients that an average adult should consume."}{"title": "REGLAMENTO 1924/2006:El Reglamento 1924/2006 regula las declaraciones nutricionales y de propiedades saludables de los alimentos en la Uni\u00f3n Europea."}{"title": "AGENCIA EUROPEA DE SEGURIDAD ALIMENTARIA:La Agencia Europea de Seguridad Alimentaria (EFSA) eval\u00faa las bases cient\u00edficas de las declaraciones sobre la salud de los alimentos."}{"title": "FACE:FACE, or Federaci\u00f3n de Asociaciones de Celiacos de Espa\u00f1a, is an organization dedicated to supporting individuals with celiac disease in Spain. It provides essential information and resources for those affected by this condition. Additionally, FACE plays a crucial role in overseeing the certification of gluten-free products across Europe, ensuring that these products comply with strict regulations regarding gluten content. Specifically, FACE is responsible for granting the European License System (ELS) certification for gluten-free products, which guarantees that items bearing its mark contain gluten levels below 10 parts per million (ppm). Through its efforts, FACE aims to enhance the safety and quality of gluten-free options available to consumers."}{"title": "CEL\u00cdACOS:Las personas cel\u00edacas son aquellas que tienen intolerancia al gluten y requieren productos espec\u00edficos para su dieta."}{"title": "GLUTEN:GLUTEN is a protein found in wheat and related grains, including certain cereals. It plays a crucial role in the elasticity of dough, making it important in baking and food production. However, gluten can cause adverse reactions in individuals with celiac disease, a condition that necessitates the complete elimination of gluten from their diet to avoid serious health complications. Additionally, gluten can trigger reactions in those with gluten sensitivity. The certification process for gluten-free products is heavily influenced by the presence of gluten, ensuring that these products meet safety standards for those affected. Recent recommendations from the European Society for Pediatric Gastroenterology, Hepatology and Nutrition (ESPGHAN) have also addressed the introduction of gluten into the diets of infants, indicating that guidelines on the timing of gluten introduction have been updated."}{"title": "DECLARACIONES NUTRICIONALES:Las declaraciones nutricionales son afirmaciones que sugieren que un alimento tiene propiedades beneficiosas espec\u00edficas debido a su composici\u00f3n."}{"title": "DECLARACIONES DE PROPIEDADES SALUDABLES:Las declaraciones de propiedades saludables afirman o sugieren una relaci\u00f3n entre un alimento y la salud."}{"title": "DECLARACIONES DE REDUCCI\u00d3N DE RIESGO:Las declaraciones de reducci\u00f3n de riesgo afirman que el consumo de un alimento puede reducir significativamente un factor de riesgo de aparici\u00f3n de una enfermedad."}{"title": "REGULACI\u00d3N NUTRICIONAL:"}{"title": "AOECS:The AOECS, or Association of European Coeliacs, is an organization dedicated to regulating the use of the gluten-free symbol and certifying gluten-free products throughout Europe. It oversees the certification process across its member associations, ensuring that products meet the necessary standards for gluten-free labeling. The AOECS plays a crucial role in supporting individuals with celiac disease by providing assurance regarding the safety and quality of gluten-free products available in the market."}{"title": "SPIGA BARRADA:Spiga barrada is the international symbol for gluten-free products, regulated by AOECS and used by industries to signify compliance with gluten-free standards."}{"title": "EUROPEAN REGULATIONS:European regulations govern the labeling and production standards for both ecological and organic products across member states. These regulations include specific guidelines for gluten-free certifications, ensuring that products meet established criteria for quality and safety."}{"title": "PRODUCTS ECOLOGICAL:Ecological products are those that meet specific European standards for organic production and labeling, including gluten-free requirements."}{"title": "GLUTEN-FREE SYMBOL:"}{"title": "ASOCIACI\u00d3N DE CEL\u00cdACOS ITALIANA:The Italian Celiac Association is responsible for granting ELS certification in Italy for gluten-free products."}{"title": "EUROPEAN LICENSE SYSTEM:The European License System (ELS) is a certification process that allows industries to use the gluten-free symbol, regulated by AOECS."}{"title": "ITALY:Italy is a country located in Europe known for its rich cultural heritage and significant contributions to various fields, including health and nutrition. Research conducted in Italy has focused on dietary antioxidant capacity and its relationship with cancer risk, highlighting the country's commitment to advancing public health knowledge. Additionally, Italy is home to the Italian Celiac Association, which plays a crucial role in promoting gluten-free products by granting ELS certification, ensuring that consumers have access to safe and reliable food options."}{"title": "ECOLOGICAL PRODUCTS:Ecological products are those produced without synthetic chemicals and certified by a control organism, adhering to strict regulations."}{"title": "AGRICULTURAL PRODUCTS:Agricultural products refer to items produced from farming, which can be classified as ecological based on their production methods."}{"title": "ECOLOGICAL LABELING:Ecological labeling refers to the regulations and standards that products must meet to be labeled as ecological, ensuring they are not misleading to consumers."}{"title": "ECOLOGICAL FARMING:Ecological farming is a method of agriculture that avoids synthetic chemicals and respects natural growth rhythms."}{"title": "PRODUCTS IN CONVERSION:Products in conversion are those that are in the process of transitioning to ecological farming and cannot yet be labeled as ecological."}{"title": "ECOLOGICAL INGREDIENTS:Ecological ingredients are components of food products that are produced according to ecological standards."}{"title": "ECOLOGICAL CERTIFICATION:Ecological certification is the process by which products are verified to meet ecological standards by a recognized control organism."}{"title": "EUROPEAN ORGANIC CERTIFICATION ENTITY:An organization that certifies products as organic according to EU standards, ensuring compliance with regulations for organic labeling."}{"title": "EGGS:Eggs are a common dietary item that have been extensively studied for their potential impact on cholesterol levels and cardiovascular risk. Additionally, they are subject to specific regulations that require proper labeling concerning their production methods and origin. This ensures that consumers are informed about the quality and source of the eggs they purchase."}{"title": "DENOMINATION OF ORIGIN PROTECTED:A quality label that indicates that a product comes from a specific geographical area and meets certain quality standards."}{"title": "INDICATION OF GEOGRAPHICAL PROTECTED:A quality label that signifies that a product has a specific geographical origin and possesses qualities or a reputation due to that origin."}{"title": "TRADITIONAL SPECIALTY GUARANTEED:A label that indicates a product is recognized for its traditional production methods and characteristics."}{"title": "ORGANIC PRODUCTS:Organic products are those that are produced without synthetic fertilizers or pesticides and must adhere to specific labeling regulations in the EU."}{"title": "CONTROL BODY:A control body is an organization responsible for certifying that products meet organic standards and regulations set by the European Union."}{"title": "AGRICULTURE UE:Agriculture UE refers to products that are sourced from the European Union, indicating their origin in organic labeling."}{"title": "AGRICULTURE NON UE:Agriculture non UE refers to products that are sourced from outside the European Union, indicating their origin in organic labeling."}{"title": "AGRICULTURE UE/ NON UE:Agriculture UE/ non UE refers to products that have ingredients sourced from both the European Union and non-EU countries, indicating their origin in organic labeling."}{"title": "EUROPEAN LOGO:"}{"title": "DENOMINACI\u00d3N DE ORIGEN PROTEGIDA:Denominaci\u00f3n de Origen Protegida (DOP) identifies food products originating from a specific place, region, or country, whose quality or characteristics are fundamentally due to the geographical environment, and must be produced in that defined geographical area."}{"title": "INDICACI\u00d3N GEOGR\u00c1FICA PROTEGIDA:Indicaci\u00f3n Geogr\u00e1fica Protegida (IGP) identifies products originating from a specific place, region, or country, which possess a certain quality or reputation attributable to their geographical origin, with at least one phase of production occurring in the defined area."}{"title": "ESPECIALIDAD TRADICIONAL GARANTIZADA:Especialidad Tradicional Garantizada (ETG) protects traditional production methods and recipes, identifying specific products resulting from traditional practices, regardless of their geographical origin."}{"title": "CORDERO MANCHEGO:Cordero manchego is an example of a product that falls under Indicaci\u00f3n Geogr\u00e1fica Protegida, recognized for its specific qualities attributed to its geographical origin."}{"title": "JAM\u00d3N SERRANO:Jam\u00f3n serrano is a product that is recognized under Especialidad Tradicional Garantizada, known for its traditional production methods."}{"title": "TORTAS DE ACEITE:Tortas de aceite are traditional Spanish products that are protected under Especialidad Tradicional Garantizada for their unique production methods."}{"title": "LECHE DE GRANJA:Leche de granja is a traditional product recognized under Especialidad Tradicional Garantizada, produced using traditional methods."}{"title": "PANELLETS:Panellets are traditional sweets in Spain that are protected under Especialidad Tradicional Garantizada, made with traditional recipes."}{"title": "ENVASADO INTELIGENTE:Envasado inteligente refers to a type of food packaging that provides information about the product inside, based on the interaction between the food and the packaging."}{"title": "INDICADORES DE FRESCURA:Indicadores de frescura are devices used in smart packaging to monitor the quality of packaged food by responding to changes in the food's condition."}{"title": "DISPOSITIVOS DE TIEMPO Y TEMPERATURA:Dispositivos de tiempo y temperatura provide visual information about the cumulative effect of time and temperature on food products."}{"title": "DISPOSITIVOS DE FUGAS:Dispositivos de fugas monitor the presence or absence of oxygen in food packaging, indicating potential spoilage."}{"title": "INDICADOR DE FR\u00cdO:Indicador de fr\u00edo is a temperature indicator that changes color to show whether a product has been kept at the appropriate cold temperature."}{"title": "REGLAMENTO (CE) 510/2006:The \"REGLAMENTO (CE) 510/2006\" is a regulation focused on the protection of geographical indications and designations of origin for agricultural and food products. This regulation aims to safeguard the unique characteristics and reputation of products that are linked to specific geographical areas, ensuring that consumers are not misled about the origin of these products."}{"title": "COMISI\u00d3N DE LAS COMUNIDADES EUROPEAS:The European Commission is the executive branch of the European Union responsible for proposing legislation and implementing decisions."}IÓ0␀␀␀␀␀œÓ0␀␀␀␀␀WÔ0␀␀␀␀␀›Ô0␀␀␀␀␀J0␀␀␀␀␀wÚ0␀␀␀␀␀‚Ú0␀␀␀␀␀QÛ0␀␀␀␀␀æÛ0␀␀␀␀␀ı0␀␀␀␀␀≥˜0␀␀␀␀␀g˘0␀␀␀␀␀É˚0␀␀␀␀␀¸0␀␀␀␀␀~¸0␀␀␀␀␀Ë¸0␀␀␀␀␀P˝0␀␀␀␀␀¬˝0␀␀␀␀␀6˛0␀␀␀␀␀®˛0␀␀␀␀␀Aˇ0␀␀␀␀␀¨1␀␀␀␀␀)1␀␀␀␀␀¶1␀␀␀␀␀%1␀␀␀␀␀ì1␀␀␀␀␀˜1␀␀␀␀␀a1␀␀␀␀␀”1␀␀␀␀␀;1␀␀␀␀␀£1␀␀␀␀␀1␀␀␀␀␀ô1␀␀␀␀␀1␀␀␀␀␀ï1␀␀␀␀␀î	1␀␀␀␀␀
